{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02977",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.63,
      "end_seconds": 4.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Hello? Doctor? I was told to come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.93,
      "end_seconds": 10.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.35,
      "end_seconds": 17.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.43,
      "end_seconds": 25.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "It's my heart suddenly racing. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.1,
      "end_seconds": 29.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.19,
      "end_seconds": 35.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "About three weeks, uh, give or take."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 36.69,
      "end_seconds": 41.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Well, I think it's been nearer a month, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.1,
      "end_seconds": 46.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly three to four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.58,
      "end_seconds": 51.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "I suppose so, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.69,
      "end_seconds": 58.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.5,
      "end_seconds": 74.41,
      "duration_seconds": 14.91,
      "text": "It happens a few times a day. Cold water on the face helps a bit. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.17,
      "end_seconds": 77.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.97,
      "end_seconds": 82.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "It usually comes with it stopping just as suddenly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.18,
      "end_seconds": 90.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "Well, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 90.93,
      "end_seconds": 97.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Ah, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.74,
      "end_seconds": 107.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "I was getting to that! The, The it stopping just as suddenly? That's been for five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.39,
      "end_seconds": 112.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Any a pounding in your neck as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.76,
      "end_seconds": 119.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "Yes, since Friday. With pounding in my neck, I'd call it moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.52,
      "end_seconds": 123.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Any chest pain or breathlessness at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.56,
      "end_seconds": 138.95,
      "duration_seconds": 13.39,
      "text": "No, no chest pain, no breathlessness. I was feeling lightheaded during an episode at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.0,
      "end_seconds": 144.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "And what about fainting or family history of sudden death?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.03,
      "end_seconds": 150.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Uh, no, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.97,
      "end_seconds": 153.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.39,
      "end_seconds": 156.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.65,
      "end_seconds": 160.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.56,
      "end_seconds": 165.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.22,
      "end_seconds": 170.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.24,
      "end_seconds": 172.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.48,
      "end_seconds": 177.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.33,
      "end_seconds": 185.37,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Well, um, I take spironolactone, 25 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 186.45,
      "end_seconds": 192.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "That's what's prescribed, but I'm not sure she takes it every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.03,
      "end_seconds": 203.04,
      "duration_seconds": 10.01,
      "text": "It's gliclazide, 80 milligrams, twice a day. I take clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day for the stent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.33,
      "end_seconds": 204.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.53,
      "end_seconds": 214.58,
      "duration_seconds": 9.05,
      "text": "Uh, uh, I had furosemide at one point, but I'm off it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.29,
      "end_seconds": 218.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.73,
      "end_seconds": 222.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.69,
      "end_seconds": 234.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.62,
      "end_seconds": 246.11,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "Sorry, um, what was I saying, I've had heart failure for about a year now. I've got diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.69,
      "end_seconds": 248.39,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.54,
      "end_seconds": 258.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "Heart disease, for about ten years. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.11,
      "end_seconds": 268.23,
      "duration_seconds": 9.12,
      "text": "Yes, heart failure and heart disease are known to us, good to have that clear. Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.62,
      "end_seconds": 273.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.08,
      "end_seconds": 278.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.79,
      "end_seconds": 283.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 299.81,
      "end_seconds": 311.62,
      "duration_seconds": 11.81,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. BP is 127 over 73, temperature 36.5, respiratory rate 17, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, pulse is 70 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.16,
      "end_seconds": 314.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.04,
      "end_seconds": 320.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.24,
      "end_seconds": 322.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.44,
      "end_seconds": 339.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Your heart sounds and rhythm are normal today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.13,
      "end_seconds": 354.51,
      "duration_seconds": 12.38,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Having listened and examined, I think we're dealing with episodes of supraventricular tachycardia at this stage. Atrial fibrillation is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.96,
      "end_seconds": 359.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.57,
      "end_seconds": 373.02,
      "duration_seconds": 12.45,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now episodes of supraventricular tachycardia is my leading thought, not anything worse. I think a 7-day heart monitor makes sense here, for paroxysmal palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.55,
      "end_seconds": 375.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Right, understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.11,
      "end_seconds": 394.8,
      "duration_seconds": 17.69,
      "text": "I'm going to order a thyroid test, for palpitations. Try blowing hard against a closed mouth and nose when it starts. Do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.79,
      "end_seconds": 399.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}